  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Monday)\nIssued at 940 PM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nA strong upper trough over the Great Lakes will push a strong cold\nfront into the Ohio and Tennessee Valleys Thursday night into\nFriday. Not anticipating much in the way of rain chances with \nthis feature, but some added cloud cover may accompany it as it \npasses through the area. The main impact will be the breezy \nconditions that will be observed on Friday with the passage of the\nfront and much cooler and drier air mass that will advect into \nthe area in its wake. Highs on Friday (the transition day) will \nrun about 10 degrees lower than Wednesday/Thursday (highs in the \nlower 80s), but a strong push of cooler air will occur overnight \nas lows will drop like a rock into the mid to upper 40s by early \nSaturday morning. This autumn-like air mass will take hold on \nSaturday as highs in the upper 60s will be common on Saturday and \nthe upper 60s to lower 70s on Sunday (with lows in the 40s). As \nridging builds in, a gradual warming trend will take place as \nhighs return to the mid to upper 70s by Monday.",
